Visualizing scientific discoveries and news has never been easier. I myself take it for granted because GPT 2.5 makes it so easy but visuals like this would take me a long time to prepare just a couple of years ago. 

4 images, 4:5, do research, do this for 4 scientific discoveries of the past month: INPUT: $ TOPIC
// Semantic inference
EVENT = infer_event_type($ TOPIC)             // conference, symposium, retrospective, expo
TITLE = derive_display_word($ TOPIC, 6..14)   // ALL CAPS condensed black
SUBTITLE = infer_subtitle_line($ TOPIC)       // one sentence, uppercase, tracked
DATE = infer_significant_date($ TOPIC)        // "16 SEP 2026"
LOCATION = infer_location($ TOPIC)            // city · region
REFERENCE = infer_journal_or_publisher($ TOPIC) // "Nature 2026"
PAPER_TITLE = infer_paper_title($ TOPIC)      // small caps multi-line
THEME_WORDS = infer_theme_column($ TOPIC, 4)  // science / society / intelligence / together
HERO = infer_hero_subject($ TOPIC)            // translucent scientific specimen
LEGEND = infer_legend_system($ TOPIC, 2..3)   // color-coded tissue/system keys
MICROGRAPHS = infer_micrograph_set($ TOPIC, 3) // detail views with scale bars
ORIENTATION = infer_orientation_keys($ TOPIC) // A-P, D-V, L-R
FOOTER = infer_footer_tagline($ TOPIC)        // e.g. "MINDS EXTEND"

// Build a poster potential field Φ.
Φ = hero_gravity(HERO) + title_weight(TITLE) + grid_columns(4)
F = ∇Φ       // reading flow: header → title → hero → columns → strip
Curl = ∇×Φ   // organic curves of the hero specimen, micrograph cells
Div = ∇·F    // density of annotations, scale bars, callouts

// COMPOSITION:
// - Full‑width header: EVENT line left, secondary metadata right.
// - TITLE: massive condensed black caps, 90% width, single line.
// - SUBTITLE: tracked uppercase, centered under title.
// - Left column: DATE (huge numerals) + LOCATION + THEME_WORDS.
// - Right column: REFERENCE + PAPER_TITLE + ORIENTATION key.
// - Center hero: translucent X‑ray style specimen, blue/white gradient, glows.
// - Callouts: thin leader lines with small caps labels.
// - Legend: bottom‑left, color squares + uppercase labels.
// - Bottom strip: 3 micrographs with labels + scale bars + a diagram key.
// - Footer: spaced small caps tagline, centered.

// STYLE:
// - Off‑white paper background, editorial print.
// - Blue/white/gray scientific palette with warm accent if needed.
// - Photorealistic specimen render (scientific illustration aesthetic).
// - No cartoon, no neon, no decorative clutter.
// - Clean Swiss grid with asymmetric editorial balance.

// FINISH:
// - Reads as a genuine conference poster.
// - Title legible at thumbnail; micrographs reward close inspection.
Render 3:4 or 4:5, 8K.
